Healthy Breakfast Ideas for Period Days

Breakfast can be an important meal when you are on your period, especially if you wake up feeling hungry, tired, or low on energy. A nutritious breakfast does not need to take a lot of time. With a few simple ingredients, you can prepare meals that are filling and enjoyable.

Oatmeal is one easy option. Cook oats with milk or a suitable plant-based alternative and add banana, apple, berries, nuts, or seeds. Oats provide carbohydrates and fibre, while nuts and seeds add healthy fats and some protein. You can change the toppings every day to keep breakfast interesting.

If you prefer savoury foods, eggs with whole-grain toast and vegetables can be a simple combination. Eggs provide protein, while vegetables add fibre and important micronutrients. You could also make an omelette with spinach, tomatoes, onions, and other vegetables you enjoy.

Indian breakfast foods can also fit perfectly into a balanced period diet. Idli with sambar provides carbohydrates, vegetables, and lentils. Vegetable poha can be prepared with peas, carrots, peanuts, and other vegetables. Upma can also be made with plenty of vegetables and served with yoghurt or another side.

A fruit and yoghurt bowl is useful on mornings when you do not want a heavy meal. Add banana, papaya, berries, apple, or another fruit to yoghurt and top it with oats, chia seeds, almonds, or pumpkin seeds. This can provide a combination of carbohydrates, protein, and healthy fats.

If you are short on time, a smoothie can be another option. Blend banana with yoghurt or milk and add oats, peanut butter, or seeds for extra staying power. You can also include fruits such as berries or papaya.

Iron is worth considering throughout your diet because menstruation involves blood loss. Foods such as lentils, beans, spinach, chickpeas, tofu, eggs, and meat can contribute iron. Adding vitamin C-rich foods alongside plant-based sources can help with iron absorption.

Do not forget to drink water after waking up and throughout the morning. Hydration is an important part of your everyday routine.

